  ('5dc6943d-62be-5bd7-81a2-cdbdb71fb861', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-figurative-language'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The sign "TRY OUR CORNY JOKES" is a pun. Which two meanings of "corny" does it use?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Made from corn, and sold at a very cheap price","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"invented-meaning"},{"text":"Made from corn, and silly in a way that makes people groan","is_correct":true},{"text":"Grown on a farm, and baked fresh that same morning","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"Silly in a way that makes people groan, and very sweet","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"invented-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Made from corn, and silly in a way that makes people groan$q$, $q$The muffins are corn muffins, and a "corny" joke is a silly one that makes people groan, so the word fits both. Nothing in the word "corny" means cheap, so that choice only gets half of the pun right.$q$, 'draft', '80735e54-7cea-5d0d-b576-3115f19803a0')
