  ('abd0c57c-6e45-5888-bbf6-c2f9aaf5a16f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$At the end, Aiyana says, "Next year, we should order rain on purpose." How does this line connect to Tomas's earlier words "Just the weather I ordered"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She is warning him that bad weather will ruin next year's sale.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She is reminding him that he really did ask for rain that day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"She echoes his sarcastic line, but now wanting rain seems reasonable.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She repeats his line to show she is still upset about the rain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-tone-shift"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She echoes his sarcastic line, but now wanting rain seems reasonable.$q$, $q$Tomas's first "ordered" was ironic because the rain seemed to ruin everything, but the rain ended up bringing customers inside, so Aiyana's joke turns the idea into something they might actually want. She is smiling about their success, not still upset.$q$, 'draft', '80735e54-7cea-5d0d-b576-3115f19803a0')
