   $q$Rohan was called "chatty," and Lucia was called "articulate." What does Lucia mean by "Same idea. Different flavor."?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The words describe food, so the comment is about snacks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The words have opposite meanings, so the judges disagreed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-synonym-antonym"},{"text":"Both words describe a talker, but one praises and one criticizes.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Both words are compliments that mean exactly the same thing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-connotation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Both words describe a talker, but one praises and one criticizes.$q$, $q$Both words describe someone who speaks easily, but "articulate" praises clear speech while "chatty" suggests talking a lot about little. Lucia says "Same idea," so she does not think they are opposites.$q$, 'draft', 'f94e5168-e149-5020-a7a6-b2ff9676ff2b')
