   $q$Rohan says that not being fully awake is "pretty strong evidence for my opponent's side." Why does this line make the room laugh?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He has secretly switched sides and now agrees with the later start.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"He is pretending to be tired so the judge will feel sorry for him.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He is admitting that Lucia's folders are better than his notes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-referent"},{"text":"His own tiredness supports the very idea he is arguing against.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$His own tiredness supports the very idea he is arguing against.$q$, $q$Lucia argued that teenagers need more sleep, and Rohan, who opposes the later start, jokes that his sleepiness proves her point. He keeps arguing against the later start afterward, so he has not switched sides.$q$, 'draft', 'f94e5168-e149-5020-a7a6-b2ff9676ff2b')
