   $q$Some residents argued that the tower was "the heart of the town." What does this metaphor suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The tower is the most expensive building in the town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The tower is shaped like a heart when seen from above.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The tower is the center of the town's life and identity.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The tower makes a beating sound every hour of the day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The tower is the center of the town's life and identity.$q$, $q$A heart is central and keeps a body alive, so the metaphor says the tower is central to the town's life. The argument is about the tower's importance, not its shape or cost.$q$, 'draft', 'fdde9a57-60d5-59d2-92d7-776db8e6d3c5')
