   $q$The historical society's sign read, "Help us make time for the tower." Why is this a pun?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It asks people to arrive at the pancake breakfast at a specific time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-double-meaning"},{"text":"It tells people to set their watches by the tower's broken clock.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It asks people to give attention to the tower and to get the clock keeping time.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It means the tower will be torn down to make room for a parking lot.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It asks people to give attention to the tower and to get the clock keeping time.$q$, $q$"Make time for" usually means set aside time and effort, and the fund drive would also let the tower tell time again, so both meanings fit. The breakfast is the event, but nothing on the sign is about arriving on time.$q$, 'draft', 'fdde9a57-60d5-59d2-92d7-776db8e6d3c5')
